WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:05.310
2020 is fast approaching, and Hollywood's
major studios have lined up a slew of projects

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.390
to compete for your filmgoing dollar.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:11.410
Some of the upcoming releases on the calendar
are highly anticipated sequels, but that isn't

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.980
all we're expecting to see.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.830
Kristen Stewart has come a long way since
Twilight.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:21.279
Only two months after appearing as Sabina
in Elizabeth Banks' 2019 Charlie's Angels

00:00:21.279 --> 00:00:25.929
reboot, Stewart is set to star in Underwater,
a film about an underwater research crew who

00:00:25.929 --> 00:00:28.910
find themselves trapped following a devastating
earthquake.

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:33.129
Although it isn't slated for release until
January 10, Underwater actually finished production

00:00:33.129 --> 00:00:39.070
back in 2017, before co-star T.J. Miller's
career was quite in the shambles it is now.

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:42.761
And as much as one may want to compare it
to other sci-fi thrillers like Alien or The

00:00:42.761 --> 00:00:46.809
Abyss, Stewart told Entertainment Weekly that
there's more to it than that.

00:00:46.809 --> 00:00:47.809
According to her:

00:00:47.809 --> 00:00:50.219
"It's a really dark, scary meditation on isolation."

00:00:50.219 --> 00:00:53.450
Stewart won't be entirely isolated in the
film, though.

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:58.719
Underwater's cast also includes Vincent Cassel,
Jessica Henwick, John Gallagher, Jr., Mamoudou

00:00:58.719 --> 00:01:00.410
Athie, and Gunner Wright.

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:06.170
It's directed by William Eubank, whose sophomore
film The Signal premiered at Sundance in 2014.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:10.791
If it feels like you're having a déjà vu
film experience with 2020's The Grudge, you

00:01:10.791 --> 00:01:11.791
aren't alone.

00:01:11.791 --> 00:01:16.490
Based on the 2002 Japanese horror movie Ju-On,
The Grudge had its first American adaptation

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:21.350
back in 2004, which starred Buffy the Vampire
Slayer herself, Sarah Michelle Gellar.

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:26.200
The 2004 Grudge was rated PG-13, likely as
a means of appealing to the largest Halloween

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.200
crowd possible.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:31.450
However, this new Grudge iteration will head
into theaters with a hard R rating.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:36.710
Starring John Cho, Andrea Riseborough, Demian
Bichir, Betty Gilpin, Lin Shaye, and Jacki

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:41.260
Weaver, The Grudge tells the story of a house
cursed by the spirit of a vengeful, deadly

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:42.260
presence.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:46.230
Rest assured, however, that although The Grudge
will center on an entirely new cast of characters,

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:50.150
there will still be some callbacks to prior
films for the long-time fans.

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:52.920
Prepare to get spooked when it arrives on
January 10.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:57.780
If Guy Ritchie's more recent genre-specific
film exploits have had you questioning his

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:00.110
appeal as a director, fear not.

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:03.390
Ritchie is getting back to his crime caper
roots with The Gentlemen, which hits theaters

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:04.890
on January 24.

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:08.700
The film's trailer seems to promise drugs,
double-crosses, classic Ritchie dialogue,

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:09.700
and duplicity.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:13.110
In other words, it sounds like a return to
form for the director of Lock, Stock and Two

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:15.320
Smoking Barrels and Snatch.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:19.590
Starring Matthew McConaughey, Charlie Hunnam,
Michelle Dockery, Henry Golding, Colin Farrell,

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:23.310
and Hugh Grant, The Gentlemen is the kind
of action film we've been wanting to see from

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:25.710
Ritchie for years.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:29.830
In the aftermath of her family's untimely
death, Stephanie Patrick, played by Blake

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:30.920
Lively, heads toward self-destruction.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:35.690
When she discovers the plane crash that killed
her loved ones was orchestrated, she takes

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:38.700
it upon herself to enact revenge upon those
responsible.

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:42.250
The Rhythm Section, which was originally supposed
to have made it into theaters at the beginning

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:47.500
of 2019, marks only the third feature for
cinematographer-turned-director Reed Moreno.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:51.340
Moreno's made a name for herself on the small
screen though, having done work on The Handmaid's

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:52.740
Tale and Billions.

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:57.090
The Rhythm Section is written by Mark Burnell,
who's adapted his own novel for the big screen.

00:02:57.090 --> 00:03:00.870
The film looks to be something between a spy
thriller and a revenge thriller, with a strong

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:01.930
female lead.

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:05.370
While Lively has done action films in the
past, this will be her first time actually

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:08.200
heading up this kind of major studio action
movie.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:12.260
Rounding out the cast are Jude Law, Sterling
K. Brown, and Richard Brake, and The Rhythm

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:16.230
Section arrives in theaters on January 31.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:19.960
The 19th century German fairy tale about a
young pair of siblings who find themselves

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:23.820
lost in the woods and end up the dinner target
of a witch has certainly seen its fair share

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.240
of film adaptations.

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:29.920
Generally speaking, none have been particularly
outstanding, and some, like 2013's Hansel

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:34.069
&amp; Gretel: Witch Hunters, have gone so far
off the rails that it's just sort of laughable.

00:03:34.069 --> 00:03:38.400
But come January 31st, we'll get a pretty
straightforward onscreen version of the story.

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:42.380
Sophia Lillis, who played the younger version
of Beverly Marsh in the It films, leads the

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:46.640
cast as Gretel, while Sam Leakey makes his
feature film debut as her younger brother

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:47.640
Hansel.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:50.750
Genre veteran Alice Krige takes on the role
of the witch, Holda.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:54.900
Gretel &amp; Hansel marks only the third film
by director Oz Perkins his previous works

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:58.220
are The Blackcoat's Daughter and I Am the
Pretty Thing That Lives in the House.

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:03.069
Aside from its character-swapped title, Gretel
&amp; Hansel looks to be an incredibly creepy,

00:04:03.069 --> 00:04:05.959
true-to-its-source-material feature.

00:04:05.959 --> 00:04:11.120
The terror of isolation is having a real moment
in the horror genre films like 2016's Hush

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:15.800
or 2019's Midsommar present a kind of fear
that's compounded by the fact that there's

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:17.700
quite literally nowhere to run to.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:21.840
So, too, does The Lodge, which centers on
soon-to-be stepmom Grace as she struggles

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:25.820
to discover the truth behind a mysterious
and terrifying presence in a snowed-in remote

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:26.820
village.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:30.220
The Lodge is as much a story about a troubled
young woman trying to make a connection with

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:34.850
her fiance's less than enthusiastic kids as
it is about the creepy monster hiding in the

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:35.850
snow storm.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:39.470
Grace has a difficult past, and it's hard
to tell how much of what's happening to her

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:41.740
in the present is a direct result of it.

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:45.300
You'll just have to see it for yourself to
find out on February 7th.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:50.560
Ben Affleck reunites with his The Accountant
director, Gavin O'Connor, for The Way Back,

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:55.100
a movie that's half an inspirational feel-good
story about a man struggling with alcoholism,

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:58.810
and half a sports drama about a high school
basketball team that's fallen from glory.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:01.780
In other words, pretty much nothing like The
Accountant.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:06.410
The Way Back is written by Brad Ingelsby,
whose previous credits include 2013's Out

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:09.010
of the Furnace and 2019's The Friend.

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:13.351
The Way Back did experience a development
hurdle back in August 2019, when the film

00:05:13.351 --> 00:05:18.230
had its original October 2019 release date
pushed back to March 6, 2020.

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:22.630
The date change gave The Way Back the opportunity
to avoid having to go up against Warner Bros.'

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:27.320
already heavy fall 2019 slate, which included
It: Chapter 2 and Joker.

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:32.940
It'll also allow the basketball-centric film
to capitalize on the start of March Madness.

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:37.650
Nearly two decades after we first saw charming,
idealistic law student Elle Woods demonstrate

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:41.830
the perfect bend and snap, Reese Witherspoon
is set to reprise one of the biggest roles

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:44.110
of her career with Legally Blonde 3.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:48.170
Witherspoon won't be the only familiar face
returning for the threequel, it seems as though

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:51.560
most of the original film's creative team
has signed on as well.

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:54.060
Currently, not a whole lot is known about
the film.

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:58.330
It's yet to secure a director, and specific
plot details are being kept under wraps.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:02.690
Chances are good that Legally Blonde 3 will
be in line with the two previous movies, centering

00:06:02.690 --> 00:06:07.850
on Elle Woods' ability to overcome adversity
through optimism, ingenuity, and sheer determination.

00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:12.030
The idea with this one is that it will most
likely focus on female empowerment, hopefully

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:15.770
introducing the franchise to a new audience
when the new installment comes out on May

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:16.770
8.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:17.770
"Harvard.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:19.400
Law school."

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:22.580
"You got into Harvard law?"

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:25.430
"What, like it's hard?"

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:30.050
Coming July 3, 2020 is Free Guy, an action
comedy directed by Stranger Things' Shawn

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:34.630
Levy and starring Ryan Reynolds, who might
be the only actor to ever play the same character

00:06:34.630 --> 00:06:37.230
twice with completely opposite results.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:41.270
Free Guy tells the story of Guy, played by
Reynolds, a bank teller who comes to find

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:45.820
out that he is a non playable background character
in a brutal and violent video game.

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:50.690
The film also stars Taika Waititi, Jodie Comer,
and Joe Keery and is written by Matt Leiberman

00:06:50.690 --> 00:06:51.690
and Zak Penn.

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:54.620
There are two big, noteworthy reunions happening
with Free Guy.

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:58.800
The first is between Keery and Levy, who have
a long-running history on Netflix's hit series

00:06:58.800 --> 00:06:59.940
Stranger Things.

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:04.030
But there's also the on-screen reunion between
Reynolds and Waititi, who appeared together

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:06.630
once before, in 2011's Green Lantern.

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:07.630
"A racetrack.

00:07:07.630 --> 00:07:12.730
That's the best you could come up with for
your first big appearance.

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:13.730
Racetrack."

00:07:13.730 --> 00:07:17.199
"Oh, I'm sorry, did I disappoint you?"

00:07:17.199 --> 00:07:21.570
Disney has a long history of adapting its
theme park rides into blockbuster movies Pirates

00:07:21.570 --> 00:07:26.470
of the Caribbean turned a 15 minute boat ride
into a film franchise that spans five films

00:07:26.470 --> 00:07:28.030
and, soon, a reboot.

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:31.830
Of course, it would only make sense for the
House of Mouse to want to expand on its ride-to-movie

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:37.100
franchise opportunities before Disney's parks
are comprised solely of movie-based attractions.

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:41.199
The Jungle Cruise ride is a favorite for weary
park goers who are looking to take a break

00:07:41.199 --> 00:07:43.580
and listen to some cheap jokes for ten minutes.

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:47.500
Meanwhile, The Jungle Cruise movie looks like
it could be another franchise hit when it

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:52.410
arrives on July 24, with a fresh spin on the
ride's cornball one-liners courtesy of star

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:53.560
Dwayne Johnson.

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:57.639
The actor was originally announced for the
film back in 2015, but development on Jungle

00:07:57.639 --> 00:08:01.860
Cruise took its time co-star Emily Blunt wasn't
cast until 2018.

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:06.100
The film's official synopsis promises to add
a supernatural element to the river-bound

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:09.050
tale, which is right up director Jaume Collet-Serra's
alley.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:14.620
He's responsible for both Orphan and the 2005
remake of House of Wax.

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:18.500
Just before Halloween 2020 hits, we'll be
getting the third installment of the Conjuring

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:20.290
Universe's flagship series.

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:25.300
Patrick Wilson and Vera Farmiga will both
reprise their roles as Ed and Lorraine Warren,

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:29.320
although James Wan, who was behind the camera
for both The Conjuring and The Conjuring 2,

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:31.919
is sitting out directorial duties this time
around.

00:08:31.919 --> 00:08:35.949
He's still on board as a producer, though,
with The Curse of La Llorona director Michael

00:08:35.949 --> 00:08:37.499
Chaves taking the helm.

00:08:37.499 --> 00:08:41.219
The Conjuring: The Devil Made Me Do It is
inspired by the first time in U.S. history

00:08:41.219 --> 00:08:44.850
that a murder suspect would claim demonic
possession as a defense.

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:48.839
That would be the story of Arne Cheyenne Johnson,
who was put on trial for the murder of his

00:08:48.839 --> 00:08:51.360
landlord following a failed exorcism attempt.

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:53.769
He claimed to have been possessed at the time
of the killing.

00:08:53.769 --> 00:08:57.439
We'll have to see if the devil really did
make him do it when The Conjuring 3 arrives

00:08:57.439 --> 00:08:59.910
on September 11.

00:08:59.910 --> 00:09:04.111
Venom may not have been a critical success,
but it wasn't long after its 2018 release

00:09:04.111 --> 00:09:07.750
that rumors began to circulate regarding the
film's inevitable sequel.

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:12.699
That was confirmed in January 2019, and by
August, Andy Serkis had signed on as the film's

00:09:12.699 --> 00:09:13.699
director.

00:09:13.699 --> 00:09:17.290
Tom Hardy, Woody Harrelson, and Michelle Williams
will all return for Sony's second round with

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:21.899
the famous Marvel symbiote, while Naomie Harris
is rumored to be taking on the role of Shriek,

00:09:21.899 --> 00:09:23.639
Carnage's deadly partner.

00:09:23.639 --> 00:09:27.589
If the rumors are true, that could mean big
things for Sony's Spider-Verse.

00:09:27.589 --> 00:09:31.950
In the comics, Shriek's team up with Carnage
ultimately led to a face-off between Spider-Man

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:34.800
and Venom, along with a whole bunch of other
superheroes.

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:38.940
How the whole thing inevitably unfolds will
likely have a lot to do with the fragile relationship

00:09:38.940 --> 00:09:40.230
between Sony and Marvel.

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:44.519
If the two studios manage to work things out,
Venom 2 could be setting up the framework

00:09:44.519 --> 00:09:48.199
for a huge crossover when it arrives in theaters
on October 2.

00:09:48.199 --> 00:09:50.309
One thing we know for sure about Venom 2:

00:09:50.309 --> 00:10:00.179
"When I get outta here, and I will, there's
gonna be carnage."

00:10:00.179 --> 00:10:04.959
When David Gordon Green and Danny McBride
rebooted the Halloween franchise in 2018,

00:10:04.959 --> 00:10:06.519
they took a huge risk.

00:10:06.519 --> 00:10:10.189
The new film retconned everything that had
happened in the franchise following the original

00:10:10.189 --> 00:10:15.100
1978 film and picked up four decades later,
in a world where former babysitter Laurie

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:19.740
Strode has spent a lifetime preparing for
another confrontation with her masked stalker.

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:23.709
But according to McBride, their leap of horror
faith could have been an even bigger one.

00:10:23.709 --> 00:10:27.449
Apparently, the pair had originally planned
to pitch two films to be shot back-to-back.

00:10:27.449 --> 00:10:31.699
They ultimately decided against it, but shortly
after Halloween opened to both critical and

00:10:31.699 --> 00:10:34.610
commercial success, two more films were confirmed.

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:38.899
Slated for October 16, Halloween Kills will
see Curtis again reprise her role as Laurie

00:10:38.899 --> 00:10:43.610
Strode, along with Judy Greer as Laurie's
daughter Karen and Andi Matichak as Laurie's

00:10:43.610 --> 00:10:44.610
granddaughter Allyson.

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:49.769
It will also bring the return of several of
the franchise's original characters: 1978

00:10:49.769 --> 00:10:53.489
babysitting charges Tommy and Lindsey are
back and all grown up, with Kyle Richards

00:10:53.489 --> 00:10:57.249
returning as Lindsey, while Anthony Michael
Hall takes the role of Tommy.

00:10:57.249 --> 00:11:01.310
Nancy Stephens and Charles Cyphers are coming
back too, reprising their respective roles

00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:04.279
of Nurse Marion Chambers and Sheriff Leigh
Brackett.

00:11:04.279 --> 00:11:06.370
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:10.050
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies are coming soon.

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:13.380
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

